		(uuid "4c2ac426-8e55-4aad-b28c-4a3c730bd9e0")
	)
	(text "NOTES\nGauge 1 = MAIN supply (R1-R8) -> A0 / GPIO36.   Gauge 2 = BACKUP supply (R9-R15) -> A1 / GPIO39.\nEach gauge: top 10k+4.7k+1k from the supply, bias 100k+22k from 3V3, bottom 22k to GND, 1M pull-down.\nDS18B20 (U1) on D2 / GPIO25 with a 4.7k pull-up (R16). The sensor cable shield is not connected.\nBreadboard tests, measured at the pin against GND (gauge 1 / gauge 2):\n   healthy: as drawn  ->  1.98 V / 1.98 V\n   sag: R1 supply wire moved from 3V3 to TP1 (SAG), so the supply comes through R7 47k  ->  1.10 V (gauge 1 only)\n   dead: supply wire unplugged, the 100k+22k bias keeps a live zero  ->  0.488 V / 0.489 V\n   broken wire: wire from the gauge to the ESP32 pin unplugged  ->  0 V / 0 V\n   (on the breadboard the 1M sits at the pin end of that wire, so a broken wire reads 0 V, not a floating value)\nPower: USB only. Nothing above 3.3 V on any pin. No mains anywhere."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 195.58 0)
